C COLLECTIONS LIBRARY - MAN PAGE TREE
======================================

This directory holds real troff/groff manual pages for the library, one
file per documented symbol.

Layout
------

    man/
      <module>/<symbol>.3   one page per raw C function or type-safe macro
      <module>/<module>.7   module overview page, where present

<module> matches the header name without the .h suffix (e.g. cvector,
chashmap, cjson); raw functions and their companion type-safe macros live
side by side in the same module directory (their names never collide, so
there is nothing to disambiguate at the filesystem level). Each page's
".TH" line still records whether it documents a function or a macro (the
fourth field reads "C Collections Library - Functions" or "... - Macros"),
and its SYNOPSIS shows the real declaration either way. A symbol that is
documented once but known by more than one name (for example
cjson_parse_mp and its cjson_parse wrapper) gets one content-bearing page
plus one or more small ".so" redirect pages, exactly like glibc/BSD man
pages handle aliases.

Viewing a page
--------------

`make install` (see the root Makefile) installs every page from here into
a real man3/man7 tree, after which plain `man cvector_create` works from
anywhere, aliases included.

Without installing, run man from inside this directory so that a page's
".so <module>/<symbol>.3" alias redirects (see above) resolve correctly;
"man -l" resolves ".so" targets relative to the current working
directory, not relative to the page's own location:

    cd man && man -l cvector/cvector_create.3
    cd man && man -l cjson/cjson_parse.3   # an alias page, .so and all

Regenerating
------------

These pages are hand-authored text, not auto-generated from source
comments; edit the relevant .3 file directly when a function's or macro's
documented behavior changes, following the surrounding pages' section
order (NAME, LIBRARY, SYNOPSIS, DESCRIPTION, PARAMETERS, RETURN VALUE,
NOTES, WARNINGS, THREAD SAFETY, EXAMPLES, SEE ALSO). Please keep new pages
ASCII only.
